        "text": "# Project Helios\nKB page ID: 227f8f01-a013-4a2f-b769-3d50f7891fa7\nPath: Project Helios (root)\nType: project | Rev: 1 | Created: 2026-11-14 | Updated: 2026-11-14 | Sources: 7 | Wiki: Synthetic KB 223deaf9 (project id d086ec71-ad6c-440d-becd-6d0ff7745ec8)\nChildren: Decision: Helios Lead Selection, Helios HX-01 Thermal Stability Screen, Helios HX-02 Buffer Blocking Optimization, Helios HX-03 Signal Artifact Characterization, Helios HX-04 Dose Response in Primary Cells, Helios HX-05 Scale-up Feasibility (Draft), Helios Q2 2024 Review\nLinked from (3 pages, by type):\n  person (2): Dana Whitfield, Maja Lindqvist\n  organization (1): Northwind Biosciences\nLinks to: Dana Whitfield\n\n[section_id=sec_charter]\n## Charter\n\nThe program exists to find a thermostable lead from the NW-200 scaffold series for oral delivery (helios-program-charter.pdf › block 1). It is headed by [[Dana Whitfield]] (helios-program-charter.pdf › block 2).\n\n[section_id=sec_budget]\n## Budget\n\nFiscal 2024 funding is USD 2.4 million, reviewed each quarter by the portfolio committee (helios-program-charter.pdf › block 3).\n\n[section_id=sec_success_criterion]\n## Success criterion\n\nA lead must keep at least 80 percent of its activity after two weeks at 40 degrees Celsius (helios-program-charter.pdf › block 4).\n\n[section_id=sec_lead_decision]\n## Lead decision  [2024-09-09]\n\nThe portfolio committee approved NW-217 as the lead on 9 September 2024 (helios-go-decision-memo.docx › block 1).\n\nSection date metadata:\n- sec_lead_decision (Lead decision): event_start=2024-09-09; date_precision=day\n\n---\nSources cited above:\n  - [artifact:upload:synthetic_kb] helios-go-decision-memo.docx\n  - [artifact:upload:synthetic_kb] helios-program-charter.pdf\n\nNote: This page is an AI-compiled summary, and the documents above are the ones its text cites. Each citation in the body names its document and the place in it (memo.pdf › p. 7), which documents read (read_file in MCP) opens. Excerpts, the section(s) each source supports or contradicts, and this page's other 5 source record(s) are NOT shown here -- run `sources Project Helios` or `provenance Project Helios` for those. Open the original before quoting or before resting a conclusion on it.",
